{
    "backstory": "Myrsos was born in the village of Kish, near the river, where his father Mannizza worked as a porter before coming to Parsa to find work. When the family moved to the town north-west of the Terrace, Myrsos began carrying loads between stores and homes, just as his father did. He remembers the journey well, the sun on the path, and how his mother Ina-Esagil-rāmât carried food for the children on her shoulders.",
    "memories": [
    ],
    "hope": "By Humban, the sun may cool and the children will have enough bread to eat.",
    "worry": "The courier came today, and I wonder if the news from the road is good or bad for the town.",
    "opinions": [
        {
            "name": "Mannizza",
            "view": "A strong man, always kind to the young ones, like a father to me."
        },
        {
            "name": "Philis",
            "view": "She is bright and talks much, like a little sister who knows the world."
        },
        {
            "name": "Nergal-ušēzib",
            "view": "A brother by blood, though he lives far, and I trust him in times of need."
        }
    ],
    "saying": "By Humban, the sun is hot and the work is heavy, but the children are safe."
}
